  "definition": "Supply chain management (SCM) is the management of the activities by which products and services are sourced, converted and delivered across the organisations of a supply chain. The Council of Supply Chain Management Professionals (CSCMP) defines it as the planning and management of all activities involved in sourcing and procurement, conversion and all logistics management activities, and states that in essence it integrates supply and demand management within and across companies.[^1]",
